  "name": "jubilant-train",
  "description": "A memory-efficient implementation of Conway's Game of Life in Rust utilizing bitset-backed spatial representations for optimized state transitions. The engine employs double-buffering for grid updates and Moore neighborhood evaluation via coordinate-to-linear index mapping with safety-conscious wrapping arithmetic. The project also provides utility components for parsing Run Length Encoded (RLE) pattern files and converting them to coordinate-based Life 1.06 specifications.",
